handing out iodine tablets in the city  of zaparisia offering some protection in  the event of a radiation leak from  europe's largest nuclear power plant 55  kilometers away  a team of international atomic energy  agency inspectors has now arrived in  ukraine on route to the nuclear site  occupied by russian soldiers since march  this is an extremely unusual event i  don't think there's been anything quite  like it in history nuclear engineer  robert kelly led similar inspection  missions in iraq in the 1990s we were in  a position to go in with  the might of the coalition behind us  in this case they're going in as guests  i believe of the russians maybe the  russians and ukrainians  and i think that they might very well be  prohibited from doing everything that  they want to do  both sides in the war are accusing the  other of shelling the plant new  independent satellite images appear to  show a hole in the roof of a building  perilously close to a reactor 100 meters  away russia publishing these photos  blaming ukraine experts say the risk of  any meltdown event is low and limited to  about 40 kilometers around the plant but  nearby concerns still remain high the  nuclear inspection mission to zaparisia  begins as ukraine announces the start of  its long-awaited counter-offensive in  the south including in the neighboring  carson region after months of  near-stalemate analysts believe this  push using weapons from the west could  determine where the war goes next if  ukraine is able to liberate hassan that  will be very important to the overall  war effort uh if russia is able to hold  on to the city and the region it could  act as a gateway for a future russian  offensive to try to take the key city of  odessa which could effectively cut  ukraine off in the black sea meanwhile  the british ministry of defense says  vladimir putin is now bypassing his  minister of defense sergey shoigu and  dealing directly with commanders if true  a further sign russia's invasion is not  going to plan redmond shannon global  news london
 

